<title>UK: Glaxo, drug stocks up on U.S. buying.</title>
<headline>Glaxo, drug stocks up on U.S. buying.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK pharmaceutical companies moved higher in early trading on Wednesday after overnight U.S. buying of the sector, traders said.</p>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome Plc was up 4-1/2p at 10.15-1/2 stg by 0704 GMT, Zeneca Group Plc was up 11p at 16.15 stg and SmithKline Beecham Plc was up 4p at 708-1/2.</p>
<p>&quot;Once again we have seen U.S. buying of our market particularly of bank and pharmaceutical stocks,&quot; said the head of equity trading at one brokerage.</p>
<p>&quot;They are after quality and yield.&quot;  </p>
<p>In New York Glaxo ADRs were up $5/8 at $31-3/4 and SmithKline ADRs were up $1-1/4 at $62-1/8.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
